# The build context is `deploy/`, deliberately.
#
# It used to be the repo root with a `deploy/Dockerfile.dockerignore` beside the
# Dockerfile. The docker CLI honours that per-Dockerfile file; wrangler does
# NOT — it falls back to the context root's `.dockerignore`, which excludes
# **/node_modules and **/.next because that is right for upstream Supabase and
# fatal for an image made entirely of the traced server.
#
# Measured in one run: the smoke test transferred 765.78 MB and served, while
# wrangler transferred 40.77 kB and shipped an image containing server.js and
# no Next. CI and Cloudflare were building different images, which is why the
# image was provably good here and dead there.
#
# Rooting the context at deploy/ removes the ambiguity: the only ignore file
# that can apply is this one.
probe/
